From 32324fa997ba8a64419c7adce35bcafdb5b42bc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:28:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): external-run cards, review round 1: remote
 2-interval rule, stale failing records, auth blocker, per-ref errors, PR
 verdict [daveey]

Review round 1 of PR #3745 (head 1de163d2) found eight blocking gaps. Each has a test in
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_external_review.py that failed on 1de163d2 and passes here.

1. Remote shell probes: a probe another host runs is judged by its synced records alone (the 5400 s
   ALIVE_EVERY allowance is gone), and the probe host writes one heartbeat record per interval when its board
   syncs. A board that does not sync keeps write-on-change with task_wake_checks.last_at as freshness, so
   test_clean_checks_do_not_append_one_event_each holds unedited. unknown > 1x, red > 2x every.
2. Staleness applies before the failing-health return: one 5xx (or 401) then a dead host goes red after two
   intervals instead of staying unknown for ever.
3. auth_failed asserts service-down.<adapter>.<scope> and wakes one probe card. A missing gh login on this
   host alone (exit 4) stays red with the hourly operator warning and wakes nobody.
4. Classification: 404/410/422 are this card's ref (probe_broken, the card is woken, no shared blocker);
   a non-rate-limit 403 is auth; the local quota guard / brake refusing our own call is rate_limited (never
   red). A red failure on a scope another card reads fine wakes that card alone.
5. PR adapter verdict: newest run per workflow, and when the base requires checks every required check must
   exist and be complete on the head before a terminal result (no early "succeeded", no stale "cancelled").
   With no required checks a success settles 60 s. Its reads take the sweep deadline and an injectable api.
7. Cases 11, 13, 14 and the E2E run real cadence with jitter, the deadline wake of an external park, a
   two-database sync and the dispatcher's own wake tick.

Also: advertising hosts come from an incremental cached read (hosts_seen) instead of a 2000-event scan on
every wait-info read; a card this host's sweep has not reached yet stays unknown (not red) for up to 4
intervals while the host is demonstrably polling.

Existing tests changed: test_kanban_external_watch case 8 (auth now wakes one probe card), case 11
(_declared_every became _cadence), case 14 (a GitHub run is read by every gateway, so the old-host case uses
shell probes); test_kanban_external_activity (the auth card needs a second card behind the blocker);
test_kanban_external_adapters and test_kanban_ci_progress_pr fakes answer the new required-checks reads.

Proof: red-run1-1de163d2.log (red on the reviewed head), 41 passed here; the reviewer's 15 probes: 14 pass,
p4 asserts the old "nobody is woken" observation.

